              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">1b70ea39-fbb5-4b4f-b613-182ce457dcd0</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">NOTES:

- Use Python 3 Script blocks for your functions.
- Import your functions and classes as: from cdf import my_function, My_class
- Don't forget to add and name your INPUT and OUTPUT parameters that match your functions correctly. If you zoom in to the Python component you will see the + sign to add and - to remove them.
- You need to attach the accurate components to your INPUT parameters: sliders for integers or floats, toggles or buttons for booleans, text for strings, Rhino geometries etc. etc. 
- If an INPUT is  a list, you need to right-click the parameter to set it as LIST access. Sometimes you need to also set the type of the INPUT by clicking TYPE HINT and selecting the correct input type.
- If you want to hide an object, right-click component and uncheck Preview. To visualize again, check Preview.
- If you get errors, READ THEM! They often tell what's wrong in a simple language. If not, copy-paste to CoPilot and don't be afraid to play around!

For more Grasshopper Help, go to:
https://developer.rhino3d.com/guides/scripting/scripting-component/#script-inputs-and-outputs</item>
                  </items>
